{
  "_comment": [
    "The one config that drives the public artifact. Public and private are two",
    "PROFILES of the same pipeline, never two codebases: `private` is a superset",
    "that keeps the internal vocabulary, `public` renames and drops. Every tuning",
    "decision that differs between the two lives here and nowhere else -- the CSV",
    "column policy, the arm vocabulary, which figures ship, and the gate that",
    "checks the result.",
    "",
    "Order of operations in export_csvs.py, per CSV:",
    "  1. drop the free-text columns outright (they carry prose, not values)",
    "  2. apply `column_rename` IN ORDER (first match wins per rule, all rules run)",
    "  3. drop any column matching `column_deny` (matched AFTER renaming, so an",
    "     arm ratio whose name merely contained 'tile' survives while the tiling",
    "     structure columns do not)",
    "  4. rewrite categorical VALUES through `value_rename`",
    "  5. assert the surviving header against `forbid` and against the kernel",
    "     denylist; a hit is an error, never a warning"
  ],
  "denylist_path": "../../docs/kernel-denylist.txt",
  "source_dir": "../../learn/pytorch_fit",
  "output_dir": "data",
  "arm_vocabulary": {
    "_comment": "The only arm names a released CSV may use.",
    "full_recompute": "recompute the whole product from scratch each step",
    "delta_baseline": "the open column-exact delta baseline",
    "block_open": "the open block-scheduled reference arm (blocksched_ref.hpp)",
    "block_open_merged": "the same arm, globally row-merged emission",
    "hst": "the closed block-scheduled arm, unversioned"
  },
  "csv_allowlist": [
